# SMA-819 final-review fix wave (one agent, all items)

Crate: crates/paigasus-helikon-providers-anthropic. Files: src/translate/request.rs, src/translate/mod.rs (tests + error texts). TDD: write each failing test first.

## F1 (Important) — ToolCall arm must not split an unfinished parallel round
Today the ToolCall arm flushes pending tool_result blocks before the fold check, unconditionally. For
  user q, asst "a", ToolCall t1, ToolCall t2, ToolResult t1, ToolCall t3, ToolResult t2, ToolResult t3
the branch sends asst[a,t1,t2], user[r1], asst[t3], user[r2,r3] → HTTP 400 (t2 unanswered). main sent asst[a,t1,t2,t3], user[r1,r2,r3] (valid).
Fix: in the ToolCall arm, when pending_tool_results is non-empty, flush it ONLY if the round is complete: every tool_use id in the last assistant message of `messages` is answered by a tool_use_id in pending_tool_results. Otherwise fold the call into that last assistant message (results stay pending). Invariant to keep: pending_tool_use and pending_tool_results are never both non-empty.
Tests (full assert_eq! on messages):
- interleaved_parallel_round_is_not_split: the item list above → [user q, asst[a, tool_use t1, t2, t3], user[tool_result t1, t2, t3]].
- parallel_round_then_second_round_alternates: asst "a", t1, t2, r1, r2, t3, r3, asst "done" (preceded by user q) → user q, asst[a,t1,t2], user[r1,r2], asst[t3], user[r3], asst[done].
- resume_shape_call_result_call_result: user q, asst "a", t1, r1, t2, r2 → user q, asst[a,t1], user[r1], asst[t2], user[r2] (valid; pin it).
- Existing Task 1 tests must still pass unchanged (tool_call_after_pending_result_does_not_fold_into_earlier_assistant, multi_round_tool_loop_without_assistant_text_alternates).

## F2 (Minor, fix) — a dropped final message of EITHER role must trigger the early error
`user q, asst "a", user "", asst ""` and `user q, asst "a", user "", asst [Reasoning]` end with asst "a" and currently pass. Rename the field `trailing_user_dropped` → `trailing_message_dropped`: true when the last conversation item (UserMessage/AssistantMessage/ToolCall/ToolResult) is a UserMessage OR AssistantMessage that produced no message, AND the last element of messages has role "assistant". Update all uses and tests. Add request.rs tests for both item lists above (flag true) and keep caller_prefill_does_not_set_flag (`user q, asst a, user "", asst b` → false).

## F3 (Minor, fix) — error texts must be correct for non-text drops too
In build_body use exactly:
- empty: "no message with content to send (empty or whitespace-only text and unsupported parts are not sent)"
- flag: "the last message has no content to send (empty or whitespace-only text and unsupported parts are not sent); the request would end with an assistant message"
Update the tests' distinct-word checks to match ("no message with content", "would end with an assistant"). Add a mod.rs test: a blank-assistant final item after a blank user (`user q, asst a, user "", asst ""`) is rejected with the flag text.

## F4 (Minor, fix) — stronger asserts in mod.rs tests
- caller_prefill_after_blank_user_is_sent: assert body["messages"] == [user[text q], asst[text a], asst[text b]].
- blank_user_after_tool_result_is_sent: assert the full body["messages"] array.
- blank_user_after_tool_result_is_sent and last_turn_cache_skips_dropped_blank_user: the tool_result block's tool_use_id is the expected id.

